  "_withdrawn_comment": [
    "Boards we CAN address and do not, with the reason. Kept here rather than",
    "deleted so the decision is visible and reversible; the collector reads",
    "'boards' only, so nothing in this list is ever fetched.",
    "",
    "2026-07-29, smartrecruiters: https://api.smartrecruiters.com/robots.txt is",
    "  'User-agent: * / Disallow: /', with an Allow for /v1/companies/ granted",
    "  to LinkedInBot alone. The endpoint answers us with a 200, which is",
    "  exactly why this is checked in code and not by whether a request works.",
    "  Restore these five entries to 'boards' if SmartRecruiters changes those",
    "  terms; the parsing and its fixture are still in place and tested.",
    "",
    "2026-07-29, workable: robots.txt allows it and the board is real — that",
    "  account held 21 open roles when it was found. But apply.workable.com",
    "  answered 429 (Cloudflare 1015) for the rest of that session, so no",
    "  payload CONTAINING POSTINGS was ever captured and the per-posting parse",
    "  has never run against real data. Shipping it would be a wired-up source",
    "  nobody has seen produce a row. Capture a fixture when the limit clears,",
    "  add it to tests/test_ats_boards.py, then move this back to 'boards'."
  ],
